/T (Joe E.)
/Contents (The hitherto most successful exoplanet detection techniques have been radial velocity measurements and transit light curves, which have been perfectly sufficient to determine the masses and radii of any planets found using these methods \(and hence classify them as gas giants or terrestrial planets\). Yet in order to determine the actual chemical compositions of their atmospheres, spectroscopic studies are necessary.)
